"""Exact original criteria and changed-condition derivations; no generic closure."""
NOTES={
'T44.01.a':('The four-column certificate keeps expected acceptance F,T,T,F separate from the faulty all-accepted observation. Input1 is consistent with both implementations and cannot establish correctness. The actual GCC/Clang assignment runs bind this table to emitted binaries.','The correct implementation with DX_CAP=8 accepts5, reproducing the admission error without an assignment defect. The environment is part of the replay contract, so source correctness alone does not identify the running configuration.',['gcc-debug-specimen-0-1-assignment','gcc-stale-config','certificates']),
'T44.01.b':('Replay hashes source, executable, separate debug file, input, configuration and cwd, and records mode, seed and finite timeout. It rejects changed executable or symbol identity before interpreting the selected failure. Every parser candidate starts in a new child and runs twice.','Changing DX_MODE changes the admitted capacity with unchanged files. The manifest mode field therefore rejects the replay; seed is separately bound and cannot share a reduction cache.',['replay']),
'T44.01.c':('Removed validation preserves each parameter; assignment changes nonzero parameters to0. Observe before/after and capacity separately. Input1 is the smallest distinguishing parameter probe; input0 has the same value under both hypotheses.','With corrupted capacity8, parameter5 stays5 but is admitted. The third probe column distinguishes this from mutation. The correct-source stale-configuration executable provides the changed-condition observation.',['certificates','gcc-stale-config']),
'T44.02.a':('Both compilers warn about assignment in a condition. Parenthesizing the assignment removes that diagnostic while preserving the all-accepted defect. Debug and release results remain distinct records with exact flags and binary hashes.','Og/O2/LTO GDB transcripts record vanished as optimized out and preserve source/machine mapping. Missing state is unknown, never a zero substituted into the causal account.',['gcc-parenthesized-build','clang-parenthesized-build','scope-O2']),
'T44.02.b':('The no-allocation DxLog holds immutable first1 and last2,3,4 with dropped1. Recording cleanup and log failure cannot overwrite the first input failure. Saturating dropped count prevents diagnostic wrap from inventing lost history.','Nested operation records keep independent first causes1 and9. A process-global first cause would conflate operation identity and requires an explicitly different policy; the original per-operation implementation does not make that claim.',['gcc-debug-core','clang-release-core']),
'T44.02.c':('All GCC/Clang debug/release and logging-on/off combinations execute validation and cleanup once. Only the diagnostic macro counter changes with logging. Required transitions occur outside optional instrumentation.','The inline logging function evaluates its counter argument even when its body discards it: final counter is macro counter+1 in every profile. This is an executed language-semantics distinction.',['gcc-release-specimen-1-0-macros','clang-debug-specimen-0-1-macros']),
'T44.03.a':('The bounded original parser recognizes bracketed A/N/T/C chunks. The same admission transition is FAIL; normal completion is PASS; malformed grammar, bounded timeout and unrelated abort are UNRESOLVED. Each classification is replayed twice in fresh children.','DX_SEED is frozen in both manifest and selected transition output. Cache scope is one reduction invocation, so a different seed cannot inherit a prior classification.',['replay']),
'T44.03.b':('dx_reduce implements subsets then complements over an ordered <=16-chunk mask, adaptive granularity, a512-entry cache and finite trial budget. The callback knows the failure; the reducer does not. The real parser callback reduces NNANNNNA to A with fixed outer brackets.','The executed balanced-tree reducer removes whole child subtrees and uses a validated leaf frontend to the same C failure oracle. It reaches [[A]], then independently checks every one-deletion neighbor. It cannot splice parent delimiters to produce the flat [A] result. Character deletion can also create unresolved unbalanced text. The certificate is local to that rewrite set, not a global tree minimum.',['replay','gcc-debug-core','certificates']),
'T44.03.c':('All256 subsets are independently classified:24 PASS,88 FAIL,144 UNRESOLVED. The [1,7,8] candidate has only UNRESOLVED single-deletion neighbors; it is1-minimal. The complete enumeration also finds cardinality2 failure [2,3], so it is not globally smallest.','Admitting two deletions adds exactly three neighbors of this three-member witness; each is checked and does not FAIL. The stronger local certificate still does not establish global minimality.',['gcc-debug-core','clang-release-core']),
'T44.04.a':('GDB stops before the fifth acquisition with used=capacity=4, displays the actual load/add/store instructions, single-steps and observes the hardware watch at used5. The original raw trajectory is1,2,3,4,5,4; the repaired trajectory is1,2,3,4,4,3. The raw release hides the prior5 if only final4 is inspected. A separate increment/clamp callback case tests symptom suppression.','The actual callback between increment and clamp records observed5 while final state is restored. The fixed path never calls that callback with an invalid committed state.',['debugger-counter','gcc-raw-history','gcc-fixed-history','gcc-debug-specimen-0-1-counter','gcc-debug-specimen-1-1-counter']),
'T44.04.b':('Selected-frame observations distinguish callee status7, caller status2 and the inner shadow11. Each value is attached to its live scope and exact stop.','The optimized inline helper appears as a logical frame sharing a physical call site with main and has status13. Its source-level frame is useful evidence but not an extra physical stack activation.',['scope-Og','scope-O2']),
'T44.04.c':('Og/O2/LTO backtraces record unavailable locals and binary identity. A backtrace is a present call-stack observation, not a complete history. The saved report keeps heap absent rather than assigning zeros.','Actual O2/LTO disassembly shows a jump from dx_tail to dx_tail_leaf. GDB may synthesize a logical tail-call frame from DWARF; that does not restore a physical caller frame. Compare raw instructions with frame display.',['scope-Og','scope-O2','scope-LTO']),
'T44.05.a':('The condition used==capacity is pure. The actual live global watch is installed and its insertion/hit state is recorded. Calling dx_acquire in a condition is rejected by the diagnostic protocol because it changes the state being investigated.','The relocation transcript records two different live addresses, deletes the old watch before free, and creates a new watch at the new live allocation. The subsequent write5 is observed without reading a stale alias.',['debugger-counter','debugger-relocate']),
'T44.05.b':('At the private-candidate marker, candidate5 already violates the capacity4 invariant while published used remains4. The watch on used stops only after the later store5. The first observed store is not the first logical invalid state.','The finite event ledger puts buffered log flush after candidate, publication and clamp. A late log is evidence of an earlier event only with its captured value/sequence; flush time cannot be substituted for transition time.',['debugger-candidate','certificates']),
'T44.05.c':('The fixture width8>4 and requested3>available2 reject the modeled hardware plan. These modeled limits are not asserted as actual host limits. Actual GDB records hardware type and successful resume/hit for bounded live watches; errors remain explicit in command records.','The actual producer-thread write to predicate is observed by an unrestricted hardware watch with thread identity and all-thread stacks. A software or thread-restricted watch would not establish equivalent coverage.',['certificates','debugger-thread-watch']),
'T44.06.a':('Og/O2 mapping receipts contain real disassembly and source annotations, with compiler flags and exact executable hashes. Statements are not treated as one-to-one instructions; the optimized value can be absent. Synthetic PC ranges remain fixture models.','LTO repeats source/PC/locals observations on its own emitted binary. The helper body may be specialized and boundaries moved; the LTO transcript and instructions, rather than a prior map, define its observations.',['mapping-Og','mapping-O2','scope-LTO']),
'T44.06.b':('The retained x86-64 ABI probe seeds RBX/RBP/R12-R15, checks restored stack and nested-call alignment and exposes the algorithm return separately. The deliberate clobber keeps lower_bound result1 but changes the preserved-register verdict; fixed code passes.','The separate Cortex-M4 Thumb/AAPCS experiment uses R4-R11 and eight-byte public-interface stack alignment. QEMU runs the deliberate R4 clobber and the fixed pair, both returning1. This selected R9 convention is explicit; it is not inherited from the x86 ABI.',['gcc-abi-0','gcc-abi-1','thumb-0','thumb-1']),
'T44.06.c':('The GDB JSON is a bounded saved observation with exact binary/symbol hashes and present PC/stack variables. It is explicitly not a native core. Omitted heap is unknown. Replay rejects mismatching image and symbols before interpreting the state.','The same source line labels do not identify a build. The manifest rejection is based on actual image/symbol digests, and the Og/O2/LTO emitted artifacts are separately hashed.',['replay','scope-Og','scope-O2']),
'T44.07.a':('Integer identity histories separately reject extent overflow, uninitialized read, post-free read and use of a pre-resize generation. Failed resize leaves generation and initialized prefix unchanged; successful resize ends the prior generation before any native stale-pointer evaluation.','A write to the other field stays within an allocated array and can be language-valid, yet violates the field contract. The semantic check detects it; extent tools alone need not.',['gcc-debug-core','certificates']),
'T44.07.b':('Separate negative/repaired ASan, UBSan and unsanitized Memcheck processes bind extent, lifetime, signed overflow and initialization reports to their build flags. The ASan initialization case can terminate silently; it does not discharge definedness.','The additional copied-value specimen propagates the uninitialized integer through a separate function before the conditional use. Memcheck with origins reports the eventual branch; repaired initialization removes it.',['gcc-asan-diagnostic-0-0','clang-ubsan-diagnostic-0-3','gcc-plain-diagnostic-0-2','clang-copied-init-0']),
'T44.07.c':('Failure injection at all three acquisition prefixes preserves publication and frees exactly the initialized resources. Length3/4/5 runs force failed resize and distinct live replacement allocation, preserve the prefix, and avoid all stale-pointer evaluation. Debug, release and instrumented controls agree.','A callback view contains an owner generation. The assessor-only hidden pair rejects an expired generation and accepts the new owner; the defective pair accepts the wrong owner82. The safe model exposes ownership escape without native post-free reads.',['gcc-debug-allocation','clang-allocation-sanitized','hidden-0','hidden-1']),
'T44.08.a':('The required event sequence advances offsets2,2,4,4,7. All64 positive partitions of seven bytes are interleaved with bounded EINTR/EAGAIN retries; the complete reconstructed bytes must match ABCDEFG. Over-report and zero progress preserve accepted offset and fail.','Scatter/gather traversal explicitly skips zero-length segments without advancing bytes or dereferencing them, preserving ABCDEFG across2,0,3,0,2 segment lengths. Read0 is an EOF boundary; writer0 is no progress under this adapter.',['gcc-debug-core','clang-release-core']),
'T44.08.b':('The injected errno seam saves ENOSPC before logging sets EIO. Owned children separately observe default SIGPIPE termination and ignored SIGPIPE returning EPIPE. The eight-slot ledger with base2 admits six acquisitions and classifies the seventh as EMFILE, not ENFILE.','pthread_mutexattr_settype returns EINVAL directly while the intentionally set errno remains ENOSPC. The caller checks the returned status rather than consulting stale errno.',['gcc-host','clang-host']),
'T44.08.c':('The Linux model releases fd generation1 despite EIO, then rejects an old ticket after generation2 reuse. No automatic native close retry is issued. The selected POSIX.1-2024 EINTR contract is documented separately.','The explicit policy selector preserves the live generation for the POSIX EINTR case and releases it for Linux EINTR. Both contracts execute as models; neither is inferred from a generic retry rule.',['gcc-debug-core','clang-release-core']),
'T44.09.a':('The finite certificate distinguishes wait-for edges from happens-before edges and unordered non-atomic conflicts. The forced opposite-lock ownership experiment captures all-thread stacks, then terminates through bounded timed waits. A possible order cycle alone is not a stopped-deadlock proof.','A timeout removes a wait edge. The actual bounded experiment therefore records a transient cycle and completion, not a permanent deadlock; ownership and timed-wait return values are retained.',['certificates','gcc-cycle','debugger-cycle']),
'T44.09.b':('The actual data-race-free schedule forces false predicate check, producer update/signal, then consumer timed wait. It times out with predicate1. The retained queue repairs the protocol by waiting/rechecking under the same mutex; whole-thread debugger stacks locate the blocked consumer.','Empty broadcasts, competing two-consumer consumption and three blocked consumers exercise rechecking. The repaired queue preserves exact once-only payload ownership across these schedules.',['gcc-lost-wake','debugger-lost','gcc-queue','clang-queue']),
'T44.09.c':('Retained producer-first, consumer-first, close/timeout and cancellation cases are rerun. The new near-wake hook permits cancellation delivery or completion before the next cancellation point, and checks the corresponding payload owner. All workers join, active count reaches0 and only then can retirement destroy synchronization objects.','Three actual waiters wake spuriously and consume three distinct queued values with a complete ownership mask14. Queue capacity3 rejects a fourth publication. Separate race-detector controls demonstrate what a data-race claim can and cannot establish about protocol progress.',['gcc-queue','clang-queue','gcc-tsan-0','gcc-tsan-1']),
'T44.10.a':('The retained basic PSP decoder validates EXC_RETURN, byte alignment, readable captured extent and frame state before reading. All short lengths reject without changing output; extended FP is rejected by the basic policy. The example recovers PC0x08000402 and pre-SP0x20001000.','The explicit extended policy accepts a ninth alignment word when xPSR alignment is set and recovers pre-SP0x20001004. The basic policy still rejects it. This is captured-data decoding, not a current physical exception.',['gcc-debug-core','clang-release-core']),
'T44.10.b':('The captured certificate derives reset Thumb PC, IRQ3 vector at0x0800004c, startup ordering and BFAR validity separately. A precise-valid capture permits the address; an imprecise capture without BFARVALID does not. Side-effect registers are not blindly polled.','A cached-MCU variant adds clean-before-device-read, descriptor publication ordering, completion/quiescence and invalidate-before-CPU-read obligations. These premises are analyzed explicitly; no cache or board observation is fabricated.',['certificates','gcc-debug-core']),
'T44.10.c':('The retained DMA driver keeps cancelling state through timeout, returns ownership only after observed idle, rejects duplicate completion and rejects old tickets after a new start. A cancellation request alone does not permit a CPU write.','The reset-epoch model refuses epoch/ownership change without quiescence; after acknowledged reset, ticket7 cannot complete epoch8. Generation overflow blocks restart. Device reset quiescence remains a named platform premise.',['gcc-debug-core','certificates']),
'T44.11.a':('Property selectors bind actual extent/lifetime ASan reports, initialization Memcheck reports, race TSan reports, static Eva paths and the exhaustive defined-narrowing semantic oracle. Repaired controls exist for each tool family. Instrumented core execution does not convert semantic disagreement into undefined behavior.','An uninstrumented dependency is outside sanitizer load/store coverage. The certificate states that its internal accesses need an instrumented rebuild or a documented gap; a clean caller-only run cannot close the dependency claim.',['gcc-asan-diagnostic-0-0','gcc-plain-diagnostic-0-2','gcc-tsan-0','eva-1','gcc-core-sanitized','certificates']),
'T44.11.b':('The wider reference enumerates all65536 u8 pairs and compares saturated min(a+b,255) with defined narrowing. Exactly32640 overflow pairs disagree. Under the declared minimum-sum ordering, first failing sum is256, without claiming a unique pair.','Checked addition returns failure for the same32640 overflow pairs and leaves sentinel777 unchanged. Successful pairs publish the wider exact sum. This variant has a different failure/output contract from saturation.',['gcc-debug-core','clang-release-core']),
'T44.11.c':('The four-element static specimen separates guarded admitted n<=4 from the weakened access a[n]. Eva and ASan point to the same n4 indexing transition; normal dynamic n3 does not reach it. The minimum bad index equals the extent4.','The weakened predicate makes the n4 path reachable while preserving the source transition. Re-running Eva reports the alarm and the explicitly reached ASan control reports it; the unreached run remains silent.',['eva-0','eva-1','gcc-unreached-1','gcc-static-reached','certificates']),
'T44.12.a':('The actual callback sees5 on the increment-then-clamp path while the repaired path rejects before publication. A final value alone cannot distinguish causal repair from symptom suppression.','The asynchronous derivation requires validation before release publication and acquire before payload observation. Atomic storage of5 would still publish an invalid state, and later clamping cannot revoke an already observed value.',['gcc-debug-specimen-0-1-counter','gcc-debug-specimen-1-1-counter','certificates']),
'T44.12.b':('The minimized A trigger, non-trigger N, malformed neighbors and timeout/crash exclusions are replayed with semantic classification. Debug/release/logging profiles, all allocation-failure prefixes and sanitized relocation controls preserve their declared ownership and result contracts.','Optimization and forced allocation relocation change execution conditions while the external API remains the same. Assertions check accepted states, byte prefixes and publication, not diagnostic wording or incidental addresses.',['replay','gcc-release-specimen-1-1-counter','clang-release-allocation','clang-allocation-sanitized']),
'T44.12.c':('DELAYED.md defines an actual independent assessment workflow: wait at least seven days, freeze learner predictions/manifest/first-state/repair before reveal, record hints, then compare to the withheld assessor oracle. Author runs establish only that the exercise works. Independent performance remains unobserved.','The withheld changed component is a callback-borrow generation boundary rather than admission capacity. Its faulty and repaired binaries are validated separately, but these author runs are never labeled independent or delayed learner evidence.',['hidden-0','hidden-1'])
}
